{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Moshe.</b> From that sin onward." "<b>Would take the tent.</b> It is present tense — he would take his tent and pitch it outside the camp. 'An excommunicated teacher — an excommunicated student' (Tanchuma)." "<b>Far.</b> Two thousand cubits, as in what is stated: ״Only let there be a distance between you and it, about two thousand cubits by measure״ (Joshua 3)." "<b>And he called it.</b> And he would call it the Tent of Meeting — it is a house of assembly for seekers of Torah." "<b>Every seeker of YHWH.</b> From here: one who seeks the face of an elder is like one who receives the face of the Shechinah (Tanchuma)." "<b>Would go out to the Tent of Meeting.</b> Like 'going out.' Another interpretation: 'And everyone who sought HaShem' — even the ministering angels, when they would inquire after the place of the Shechinah, their companions would say to them: He is in the tent of Moses."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:21.990472114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}